# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user

# Certificates & key material — never commit to the repo
Cert/
cert/
certs/
certs-de/
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
# Registration / access certificates dropped into the cert folder (any extension)
registration-certificate*

# One deliberate exception to *.crt above: the German PID TEST issuer's trust anchors. These are
# public CA certificates, carry no key material and no secret, and every wallet verifier needs
# them to trust anything at all. Anyone can fetch them from D-Trust, and
# samples/GermanPidTessioVerifier/fetch-trust-anchors.sh does exactly that and checks the chains.
# They are committed so a test run needs no download, with their fingerprints recorded next to
# them in LIESMICH.txt so their authenticity can be checked without trusting this repository.
# The exception is narrow on purpose: this one folder, this one extension.
!samples/GermanPidTessioVerifier/trust-anchors/*.crt

# Backend secrets (keystore password, registration certificate).
# The .env.example template is tracked; a filled-in .env never is.
.env
certificate-*.crt

# Local AI/agent tooling state – never belongs in the repository
.claude/
